    {
      "index": 64,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "For details on our evaluation methodology please see: deepmind.com/models/evals-methodology/gemini-3-8-flash",
      "heading": "Results",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "tag": "h2",
      "text": "Intended Usage and Limitations",
      "heading": "Intended Usage and Limitations",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Benefit and Intended Usage",
      "heading": "Benefit and Intended Usage",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Gemini 3.8 Flash is well-suited for users, developers, and enterprises, designed for cost-effective scaling of general-purpose, production-ready agents. Some use cases include: software engineering, agent tasks, and complex knowledge workflows.",
      "heading": "Benefit and Intended Usage",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Known Limitations",
      "heading": "Known Limitations",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Gemini 3.8 Flash may exhibit some of the general limitations of foundation models, such as hallucinations. In addition to this, we are continually working to improve jailbreak resistance and have recently strengthened the mitigations across Frontier Safety. There may also be occasional slowness or timeout issues. At times, the model might use more tokens to maximize performance, especially at higher effort levels.",
      "heading": "Known Limitations",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "The knowledge cutoff date for Gemini 3.8 Flash is March 2026 – users can expect updated information for some domains while in others they may experience the model’s knowledge is limited to January 2025 (in line with the Gemini 3 Model Family). For more information about known limitations, see the Gemini 3.7 Flash model card .",
      "heading": "Known Limitations",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Acceptable Usage",
      "heading": "Acceptable Usage",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "For more information about the acceptable usage for Gemini 3.7 Flash, see the Gemini 3.7 Flash model card .",
      "heading": "Acceptable Usage",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "tag": "h2",
      "text": "Ethics and Content Safety",
      "heading": "Ethics and Content Safety",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Evaluation Approach",
      "heading": "Evaluation Approach",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "For more information about the evaluation approach for Gemini 3.8 Flash, see the Gemini 3.7 Flash model card .",
      "heading": "Evaluation Approach",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Safety Policies",
      "heading": "Safety Policies",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "For more information about the safety policies for Gemini 3.8 Flash, see the Gemini 3.7 Flash model card .",
      "heading": "Safety Policies",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "tag": "h3",
      "text": "Training and Development Evaluation Results",
      "heading": "Training and Development Evaluation Results",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Results for some of the internal safety evaluations conducted during the development phase are listed below. The evaluation results are for automated evaluations and not human evaluation or red teaming. Scores are provided as an absolute percentage increase or decrease in performance compared to the indicated model, as described below.",
      "heading": "Training and Development Evaluation Results",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Overall, Gemini 3.8 Flash performs similarly to Gemini 3.7 Flash across both safety and tone, with low unjustified refusals. Safety performance across non-English languages regressed slightly relative to 3.7 Flash.",
      "heading": "Training and Development Evaluation Results",
      "isFootnote": false
    },
